        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.106,
            0.833,
            0.146
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When a pair of lines are not parallel to each other, the corresponding angles formed by a transversal can never be equal to each other."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.189,
            0.522,
            0.214
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.7 Drawing Parallel Lines"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.223,
            0.824,
            0.261
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you draw a pair of parallel lines using a ruler and a set square? Fig. 5.21 shows how you can do it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.261,
            0.847,
            0.298
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Draw a line l with a scale. By sliding your set square you can make two lines perpendicular to line l."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.298,
            0.849,
            0.353
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Are these two lines parallel to each other? How are we sure that they are parallel to each other? What angles are formed between these lines and line l?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.401,
            0.357,
            0.599,
            0.528
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.401,
                0.357,
                0.599,
                0.528
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_12_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.464,
                0.521,
                0.536,
                0.536
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 5.21"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.546,
            0.849,
            0.621
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since we used a set square, the angles measure "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "9 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . The position of the lines is different, but they make the same angle with l. If line l is seen as a transversal to the two new lines, then the corresponding angles measure "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "9 0 ^ { \\circ } ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.424,
            0.631,
            0.582,
            0.804
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.424,
                0.631,
                0.582,
                0.804
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_12_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.464,
                0.806,
                0.537,
                0.82
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 5.22"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.829,
            0.846,
            0.866
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As we know these are corresponding angles and they are equal, we can be sure that the lines are parallel."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
